Package: pdanet-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.4), adb, dnscrypt-proxy, iproute2, curl, gawk, systemd, systemd-resolved | systemd, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: redsocks, nftables
Description: PdaNet+ USB tethering desktop client
 A native GTK4/libadwaita application that shares an Android phone's Internet
 connection over USB using the PdaNet+ service, with live status, traffic
 statistics, logs and diagnostics. English and Persian (RTL) are supported.
 .
 It drives the bundled pdanet command-line tool and USB helper; privileged
 operations go through polkit (pkexec) and the application never runs as root.
 Installing, upgrading or removing this package never stops an active tunnel.
